   "title": "Prices and money",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "In buying and selling, Tagalog and Spanish numbers are **used interchangeably**. Sellers often prefer the **Spanish** numbers because they are quicker to say, which suits the fast pace of a local market. To understand market vendors, you need to know both."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The money of the Philippines is the *peso*, **piso** in Tagalog. Coins are in *centavos*, **séntimó** or **pera**. One peso is **isang piso** or simply **piso**."
